# Tunes App — Ordered Visual Studio Code Codex Implementation Prompts

Use these prompts **in order**, one at a time, in Visual Studio Code Codex **Agent mode**. Agent mode is appropriate because every workstream requires Codex to inspect the repository, edit several connected files, run checks and verify the result. Do not paste all prompts into one task.

Before Prompt 1, copy `TUNES_APP_UI_UX_AUDIT_2026.md` into the root of the actual Tunes code repository if it is not already there. The prompts are detailed enough to stand alone, but having the report beside the code gives Codex the product reasoning and route inventory behind each requirement. Also copy this prompt file into the repository if you want it versioned with the implementation work.

After each prompt:

1. Read Codex's changed-file summary and test results.
2. Open the affected screens and check them yourself.
3. Resolve any reported failures before starting the next prompt.
4. Save a Git checkpoint/commit if that is part of your normal workflow.

The prompts deliberately ask Codex to implement rather than merely propose. They also tell it to preserve current business logic and use the current component tree as the source of truth.

