## Prompt 1 — Build the semantic folk design system

```text
Work in the current Tunes App repository. Read AGENTS.md and the full UI audit in TUNES_APP_UI_UX_AUDIT_2026.md before changing anything. Inspect the current working tree and preserve all existing user changes. Treat current component names and the current file tree as the implementation source of truth. Do not edit synced reference material under sources/. Do not stop after writing a plan: implement this workstream, run appropriate checks, and report changed files, verification completed, and remaining risks. Do not begin work from later prompts.

Goal: replace the current green-dominated visual foundation with a semantic, accessible, folksy design system that can support every later redesign without rewriting business logic.

Implement the following:

1. Audit the existing global CSS variables, Tailwind theme, buttonStyles, cardStyles, form controls, badges, modals and layout primitives. Map existing tokens to semantic jobs rather than raw colour names.
2. Introduce these foundation tokens:
   - canvas parchment #F4EFE4
   - raised paper #FFFDF8
   - soft field note #E9E1D3
   - ink #25231F
   - muted ink #675F55
   - hairline #D3C7B5
   - primary umber #5B4325, hover/pressed #49351D
   - Known/Solid/success moss #68754A
   - active Practice/Reference river #466A78
   - Due/Stage/Shaky ochre #C18B32, using dark ink on filled ochre
   - Overdue/Rough/attention rust #A9533E
   - Social/community/badges plum #755B72
   - destructive oxblood #8E3934
3. Create semantic token names such as surface-canvas, surface-paper, surface-note, text-primary, text-muted, action-primary, state-known, state-practice, state-due, state-overdue, state-social and action-destructive. Components should not need to know hex values.
4. Preserve a system sans-serif stack for controls, lists and metadata. Add one warm editorial serif only for tune titles, selected section openings and badge names. Load it in a performant, privacy-conscious way and provide a robust fallback. Do not turn all body copy into serif text.
5. Define a restrained radius system: compact controls, object cards and sheets. Full pills should be reserved for statuses and one-line segmented controls. Replace “a rounded bordered card around every group” with spacing, paper surfaces and hairline dividers where possible.
6. Define elevation/material tokens. Reading surfaces must stay opaque. Translucency/backdrop blur may be used only for navigation and compact floating control layers, with an opaque fallback and support for reduced transparency/high contrast.
7. Define motion tokens around 180–260ms with restrained easing/spring-like movement. Add reduced-motion fallbacks.
8. Create or refine shared primitives: StatusMark, SectionHeader, EmptyState, RecoveryState, Skeleton/LoadingState and semantic button variants. StatusMark must combine colour, icon/shape and plain text; colour alone is never sufficient.
9. Standardise one coherent outline icon approach using an existing dependency if suitable. Do not add a large library without checking current dependencies and bundle impact.
10. Migrate the existing shared buttons, cards, form fields, tabs/segmented controls and ResponsiveModal to the new tokens so most routes inherit the design automatically. Preserve ResponsiveModal's focus trap, Escape handling, focus restoration, safe-area behaviour and body locking.
11. Remove hard-coded olive/green values from shared components where a semantic token should be used. Do not mechanically replace legitimate content colours.

Acceptance criteria:

- The app builds and its existing tests pass.
- Core text and semantic colours meet WCAG AA contrast in their intended pairings.
- Rough, Shaky, Solid, Known, Stage, social and destructive states are visually distinguishable and understandable without colour.
- Light surfaces feel like parchment/paper rather than pale green panels.
- Existing functionality and route behaviour remain intact.
- Reduced-motion and reduced-transparency preferences have usable fallbacks.
- Provide before/after screenshots of representative Home, Tunes, Practice, Lists and Social screens at phone and desktop sizes, or add a small internal design-system preview route if that is the repository's established approach.
```

