## Prompt 2 — Rebuild the responsive app shell and navigation

```text
Work in the current Tunes App repository after Prompt 1 has been completed. Read AGENTS.md and TUNES_APP_UI_UX_AUDIT_2026.md, inspect the current working tree, and preserve existing changes. Treat the current file tree and names as authoritative. Do not edit sources/. Implement this workstream completely, test it, and report changed files and verification. Do not begin later workstreams.

Goal: replace the crowded phone header navigation and underused desktop layout with an adaptive app shell that is reachable, stable and native to Tunes.

Implement the following:

1. Replace the signed-in phone navigation grid with a bottom NavigationDock containing exactly five primary destinations: Home, Practice, Tunes, Lists and Social. Use icon plus short label. Make the entire target at least 44x44 CSS pixels and clearly identify the selected destination.
2. Add a compact phone top bar containing the current page title, at most one relevant page action/search affordance, and the signed-in person's avatar/account button. Do not repeat the large brand/tagline on every signed-in screen.
3. Move Account, Settings, Help/Feedback and other secondary destinations behind the avatar/account menu. Moderator and Dev must only appear for authorised roles and must not appear in ordinary consumer navigation.
4. Menus and navigation groups must overlay/anchor from the control that opened them; they must not push the current page down. Use the existing accessible modal/popover foundations where appropriate.
5. Respect bottom safe areas and ensure page content cannot be obscured by the dock. Avoid double padding when later SessionDock controls are present.
6. Allow the phone dock to become more compact while scrolling down, without removing the selected destination or making navigation hard to rediscover. Restore it on upward scroll, focus or route change. Respect reduced motion.
7. Rebuild desktop navigation as a narrow persistent left rail that can collapse to icons at medium widths. Preserve room for a main workspace and optional contextual right panel. At tablet widths, let the bottom dock transition into a side rail when there is enough space.
8. Route selection must work for nested pages such as tune detail, reference media, list detail, diary, profiles and comparison. Browser back/forward navigation must remain correct.
9. Signed-out routes should have a separate simple shell. A signed-in person who reaches /login should not see a contradictory signed-in navigation/login combination; leave the final redirect/account-switch behaviour for Prompt 15 but ensure the shell does not duplicate itself.
10. Make keyboard focus order logical, include visible focus states, add accessible names to icon controls and avoid focus being hidden behind fixed navigation.
11. Preserve the strong phone Home switcher at `/` but refine its three views as part of the new shell:
   - Today leads with one Continue object: resume an interrupted session or show the most useful due tune and a short queue preview.
   - Repertoire shows compact counts and recent changes rather than another full catalogue.
   - Social keeps compact events and collapsed comments; its deeper feed will be completed in Prompt 12.
   Persist the selected Home view, reduce repeated introductory copy for returning users, and keep first-use guidance available through Help/empty states.

Acceptance criteria:

- All five destinations are reachable with one thumb from every ordinary signed-in phone page.
- No primary navigation target is smaller than 44x44.
- Opening navigation/account menus does not reflow the page.
- Current route highlighting works on all nested routes.
- Phone, tablet and desktop layouts do not overlap content at 390, 430, 768, 1024 and 1440px widths.
- Signed-out and internal states do not inherit inappropriate consumer navigation.
- Home Today/Repertoire/Social remain fast, persist selection and present the next useful action within the first phone viewport.
- Existing auth and business behaviour is preserved.
- Build, lint/type checks and relevant navigation tests pass; verify the shell on representative routes in a real browser.
```

