## Prompt 18 — Final accessibility, performance, offline-resilience and QA hardening

```text
Work in the current Tunes App repository after Prompts 1–17. Read AGENTS.md and the full audit, inspect all accumulated changes, preserve business logic and do not edit sources/. This is the final cross-cutting hardening pass. Fix verified issues rather than merely producing an audit. Run the broadest practical automated and real-browser verification and clearly report anything that remains.

Goal: ensure the redesigned app is accessible, fast, resilient and consistent across every reachable route and important state.

Accessibility and semantics:

1. Audit all interactive cards. Eliminate role=link/card wrappers containing nested links or buttons. Use either one whole-object link with no nested actions or a non-interactive container with explicit title/action controls.
2. Verify 44x44 primary phone targets, adequate spacing, visible focus, logical keyboard order, skip/landmark structure and headings.
3. Give icon buttons, pager controls, charts, media/loop controls, rating controls and dock states meaningful accessible names and state announcements.
4. Test zoom/text scaling, VoiceOver/screen-reader semantics where tooling permits, keyboard-only use, grayscale, increased contrast, reduced transparency and reduced motion.
5. Recheck contrast for every semantic token and component state. Borders cannot be the only cue when their contrast is low.

Performance and data:

6. Confirm Catalogue, Known, Practice, Learning Queue, Profiles, Compare, Trends and social feeds use bounded queries and bounded DOMs. Remove N+1 lookups, duplicate mobile/desktop fetches and eager non-visible media.
7. Add performance budgets/measurements for initial JS, route response, query count, rendered interactive nodes and key interaction latency. Record representative before/after numbers.
8. Add skeleton/loading, empty, retry, offline, expired and permission-recovery states consistently across routes.

Offline/resilience:

9. If the current stack supports it safely, add an installable web-app manifest and a conservative service-worker/offline shell. Cache only versioned app assets and authorised essential data needed for the active practice queue, active setlist, tune identity, notes drafts and recent diary context.
10. Never cache third-party protected media or private cross-user data indiscriminately. Provide clear pending-sync, synced, conflict and failed states. Make logout/account switch purge or isolate private caches correctly.
11. Make the active setlist and current practice position resilient to poor reception while preserving server truth and avoiding silent data loss.

Consistency and product language:

12. Sweep all visible copy for current source-of-truth names and use exactly Start Practice, Already in practice and Stage. Display Focus areas rather than Foci. Map legacy component/doc names rather than rewriting historical documents.
13. Confirm semantic colours have one stable job: moss Known/Solid, river Practice/Reference, ochre Due/Stage/Shaky, rust Overdue/Rough, plum Social/Badges and oxblood destructive.
14. Verify every empty, missing, expired, private and invalid state offers a safe useful next action without leaking private existence.

Testing and measurement:

15. Run formatter, lint, type check, unit/integration tests and production build. Fix new warnings and console errors.
16. Add or update end-to-end coverage for signed-out login, Home tabs, Catalogue/search/filter/create/add-to-list, Known, Practice and catch-up, Tune Detail, Reference Media, Lists variants/public lists, Diary Day/Week/Month, Focus areas, Friends, Inbox, Compare/in-person invalid states, Trends/style detail, Badges, Setlists/Performance, Profiles, Dashboard and authorised/unauthorised internal tools.
17. Run the route matrix at small phone, large phone, tablet portrait/landscape and desktop. Check overlays, safe areas, scrolling, keyboard focus and browser back/forward. Capture failures and fix them.
18. Where analytics already exists and consent/privacy permit it, instrument the audit's success measures: time to first practice rating, tunes per practice session, time to find a tune, filter abandonment, Tune Detail to Reference/Practice conversion, Compare-to-setlist conversion and interaction latency. Do not add invasive tracking merely to satisfy this item.

Final acceptance criteria:

- Production build and test suite pass with no new console errors.
- Core phone tasks can be completed one-handed without controls covering content.
- No ordinary list renders hundreds of interactive objects at once.
- Core workflows work by keyboard and expose meaningful screen-reader structure.
- Offline/private-cache behaviour is safe, explicit and account-isolated, or the completion report clearly explains why a smaller resilience implementation was chosen.
- Provide a final route-by-route pass/fail matrix, changed-file summary, performance comparison, known limitations and recommended post-release monitoring. Do not claim completion for any unverified route.
```

